. And we have, joining company with these prime monkeys headed by Angada, come to the South, protected by Yama, and inhabited by Agastya.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4091e55a0ebf3379a1bbe3cd144337766f1a6cb1179fc7205109363e1b8fa1fe","compact":"4fe01126de42fbe694b5076eeceede53949fe14d98754b49befcc13d8c93ea4f","nasal":"4fe01126de42fbe694b5076eeceede53949fe14d98754b49befcc13d8c93ea4f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":7,"english":"His friend is that heroic king, the monkey named Sugrīva. By that monarch of the foremnost monkeys have we been despatched (hither). And we have, joining company with these prime monkeys headed by Angada, come to the South, protected by Yama, and inhabited by Agastya.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2fde4b3803487105a0f2f0ef78e178e70896c71353ff406aa359696ae7edb664","compact":"ef1d34b217109a7c809cf04b35f7cfd512065e655ccf540f82a26dca0895048e","nasal":"c440de53813b3c7feb8827859011d8fca626926652cdc01b677ebbf53d8bbce1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":8,"english":"And we have been commissioned, 'Do you all search for the Rākşasa Rāvana, wearing forms at will, along with Videha's daughter, Sītā.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63c9565964144341a30991c5fcf27fa2d34db6d68b5b55d72d619ae76d94d8ad","compact":"e5ecdcc10ac65a976ee19d7eb7d06da6953c9fdcd26ff80cfa3d4776f337f17e","nasal":"e5ecdcc10ac65a976ee19d7eb7d06da6953c9fdcd26ff80cfa3d4776f337f17e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":9,"english":"Having searched through the forest as well as the ocean on the South, we becoming hungry, sat down at the foot of a tree.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.352,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83e929ccb1c4c9e450663b620e4a479443e78ceb053b90721fbaa1b40286707f","compact":"15434abe77ac1661009c3c9ddf76781cb4b04c835907b1335b557b89ef51e9a8","nasal":"e8c8c76e0f461f6a25fe840538c1fadcf40285af618b23c2f1184ecf76dc0243"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":10,"english":"And with pallid countenance, we all, absorbed in thought, sank in a wide sea of anxiety, which we could not cross.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21b7f50558149087325dc3e4d441d940be96a6ad1b09326d08fc72ca9efe2cea","compact":"c725f09c637ef05e64cc529b5d4dfec2f74ca38125e29976a540b9e9869409ce","nasal":"e8638aa9d643c1c2cd0e9fc559f0c4f8dc2b51632513d70df1c77bcdecb9b299"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":11,"english":"And casting our eyes around, we spyed a huge cave covered with trees and plants and enveloped in gloom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e172a7d912f409dd11f3416a13161bf289a80700b791d418fee1016c6c7e81c","compact":"970b6c6a1de0dc90d3784ef96ab1664c1c717cac4da41fab18454a990614bbb7","nasal":"79b669df9094e4e3287badbb821bbd0f25a9f5708f5a95c2b75c7b971113ad28"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":12,"english":"And (it came to pass that) from this (cave) came out swans, drenched with water, with drops of water on their wings,-and plumed kuravas and cranes. Let us enter here', said I to the monkeys. And they also arrived at that conclusion.* And thereupon they, bestirring themselves, entered into the cave. And firmly griping each other's hands, they at once made entry into the cave covered with darkness. This is our errand; and it is on this job that we have come. *Namely, that water was to be found there.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.596,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-10","DUTT-4-52-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"297fcdba4c95eb4c78a9f160d61360f3f3f3c6ba2ca032e59e522683ac5a4416","compact":"e8e543ac045583a9809aeff3b6b9a1e61bbc92d01b03c30d8d9dbaa25f66a2dd","nasal":"04a29b33d777aa1df254245f06998a8ab6b179c168a50cc100558d153611e97c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-51-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":51,"verse":13,"english":"Let us enter here', said I to the monkeys. And they also arrived at that conclusion.* And thereupon they, bestirring themselves, entered into the cave. And firmly griping each other's hands, they at once made entry into the cave covered with darkness. This is our errand; and it is on this job that we have come. *Namely, that water was to be found there.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.46,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-52-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4051013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 189